{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Before the aged you shall rise.</b> One might think before an elderly ignoramus — Scripture says, \"זָקֵן\" (zaqen) — זָקֵן means none other than one who has acquired wisdom (קָנָה חָכְמָה); this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 19:32). And the language of Torat Kohanim (chapter 7, paragraph 11), which is what is cited in the Gemara in tractate Kiddushin (32b): Scripture says, \"זָקֵן\" — זָקֵן means none other than a sage, as it is stated (Numbers 11:16), \"Gather for Me seventy men from the elders of Israel.\" And Rabbi Yosi HaGelili says: זָקֵן means none other than one who has acquired wisdom, as it is stated (Proverbs 8:22), \"HaShem acquired me (קָנָנִי) at the beginning of His way.\" Now according to both of them, the commandment applies only to a sage. And Onkelos (Onkelos on Leviticus 19:32) said: \"מִן קֳדָם דְּסָבַר בְּאוֹרָיְתָא תָּקוּם וְתֶהְדַּר אַפֵּי סָבָא\" (\"Before one wise in the Law you shall rise and honor the face of the aged\"), and the implication of his words is that he too is of this opinion. Yet despite all this, what emerges from the Gemara according to the final halakhic ruling is not so, for they said (Kiddushin 32b): Isi ben Yehuda says, every aged person is included in the meaning, and Rabbi Yohanan said (ibid. 33a): the halakhah follows Isi ben Yehuda. Thus it commands concerning every aged person, even an ignoramus who is a boor, and then it turns back and commands concerning the zaqen, who is the one who has acquired wisdom, even a youth who is wise. And it is possible that this is also the view of Onkelos, but he translates a youth who is wise as שֵׂיבָה (seivah), because the term זָקֵן comes and reveals through שֵׂיבָה that included within it are all types of seniority — both the seniority of Torah and the seniority of years."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The Aramaic quotation from Onkelos is rendered literally without vocalization as it appears in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:56:50.835186076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}